  "question": {
    "text": "Chlorine reacts with hot and concentrated NaOH and produces compounds (P) and (Q). Compound (P) gives white precipitate with silver nitrate solution. The average bond order between Cl and O atoms in (Q) is Report your answer up to two decimal places.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1.67",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mtext>3C</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mtext>6NaOH</mtext><mo>→</mo><mn>5</mn><mtext>NaCl</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>NaCl</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mtext>3</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>NaCl</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext> </mtext><msub> <mrow> <mtext>AgNO</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <mo>→</mo><munder> <mrow> <mtext>AgCl</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mtext>White</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>ppt</mtext></mrow> </munder> <mtext> </mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext> </mtext><msub> <mrow> <mtext>NaNO</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math><br />Q is <math><mtext>NaCl</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mtext>Cl</mtext><msubsup><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-09-04_at_2.26.53_PM.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 111px;\" /><br />Bond order <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1.67</mn></math>",
